-- title:
--   Residual attachment from realisation supply at level M
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a Frey package: nonzero integers $a,b,c$, a prime $p\ge 5$ with $a^p+b^p=c^p$, $\gcd(a,b)=1$, $a\equiv 3 \pmod 4$ and $b\equiv 0\pmod 2$; and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number. The degree-zero Picard group $J_0(M)=$ `JZero M` of the modular function field at level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is equipped with the `HeckeAlg`-module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar M`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82), i.e. the module structure over $\mathbb{Z}[T_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ in which the generator at $\ell$ acts by the divisorial operator `heckeOperatorBar` when these operators commute with one another, and by zero otherwise. The theorem asserts the implication: if (i) [`ModularCurve.FrobeniusQuadraticConcrete M P.p`](def/ModularCurve_AttachmentConcrete.html#L18) holds, that is, for every prime $\ell\nmid Mp$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, every $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ that is a Frobenius at $A$ for $\ell$ (acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^\ell$) and every $x\in J_0(M)$ killed by some power of $p$ one has $\sigma\cdot\sigma\cdot x - T_\ell\cdot(\sigma\cdot x) + \ell\, x = 0$, and (ii) `P.EigenformRealizationSupplyFieldAt M` holds, that is, for every weight-two cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ that is a normalised eigenform ($a_1(g)=1$, multiplicativity of the $q$-coefficients at coprime indices, and the usual prime-power recursions according as the prime divides $M$ or not) and every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}=\mathrm{integralClosure}\ \mathbb{Z}\ \mathbb{C}$ containing $p$, there are a field $k$ with $p=0$ in $k$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the Hecke polynomial ring to $k$, a $k$-vector space $V$, a map $\pi\colon J_0(M)\to V$, a homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{GL}_k(V)$, a ring homomorphism $\psi\colon\overline{\mathbb{Z}}\to k$, and a Galois number field $F$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that the predicates `IsResidualRealization` (for $p$, $J_0(M)$, $k$, $\varphi$, $V$, $\pi$, $\rho$) and `CyclotomicDeterminant` (for $M$, $p$, $\rho$) hold, $\mathfrak{m}\subseteq\ker\psi$, for every prime $\ell\nmid Mp$ there is $a\in\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ with $a=a_\ell(g)$ in $\mathbb{C}$ and $\varphi(T_\ell)=\psi(a)$, and the kernel of restriction to $F$ is contained in the intersection of the kernel of the Galois action on the $p$-torsion of the Frey curve `P.freyCurve` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ker\rho$; then (iii) `P.EigenformResidualAttachmentAt M` holds: for every such $g$ and every such $\mathfrak{m}$ there exist a field $K$ of characteristic $p$, a $K$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_K V = 2$, a representation $\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on $V$, a ring homomorphism $\psi\colon\overline{\mathbb{Z}}\to K$ with $\mathfrak{m}\subseteq\ker\psi$, and a Galois number field $F$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose associated restriction kernel lies in the intersection of the kernels of the mod-$p$ Frey-curve action and of $\rho$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\ne p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit and every Frobenius $\tau$ at $A$ for $\ell$, there is $a\in\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ with $a = a_\ell(g)$ in $\mathbb{C}$ and $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\tau)=\psi(a)$, and moreover $\det\rho(\tau)=\ell$ in $K$.
--
--   This is the gluing step of the Eichler–Shimura construction of mod-$p$ Galois representations attached to weight-two eigenforms on $\Gamma_0(M)$: the quadratic Frobenius relation on the $p$-power torsion of $J_0(M)$ together with a two-dimensional residual realisation over a field of characteristic $p$ yields the Frobenius traces $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell)=\psi(a_\ell(g))$ and determinants $\ell$ away from $M$ and $p$. The trace clause is obtained from the relation and the determinant by the rank-two Cayley–Hamilton identity [`Module.End.trace_eq_of_mul_self_sub_smul_add_smul_eq_zero`](thm.html#Module.End.trace_eq_of_mul_self_sub_smul_add_smul_eq_zero); the result is used by [`FreyPackage.eigenformResidualAttachmentAtFamily`](thm.html#FreyPackage.eigenformResidualAttachmentAtFamily), which supplies the residual representations entering level lowering for the Frey curve.
